@startuml hu-09-domain
title HU-09 — Dominio: dónde vive cada pieza

package "Combat" #EEF5FF {
  class ExperienceRollPolicy <<política pura>> {
    + rollFor(sequence) : 1..8
    ..no conoce la fórmula..
  }
  class ExperienceRoll <<persistido>> {
    + operationId : string (clave _id)
    + roll : 1..8
    + simulationId : string
    + heroId : string
    + rivalRef : string
    + persistedAt : Date
  }
  ExperienceRollPolicy ..> ExperienceRoll : produce
}

package "Missions" #EFFAEF {
  class ExperienceReward <<agregado>> {
    + enrollmentId : string
    + simulationId : string
    + playerId : string
    + heroId : string
    + rivalRef : string
    + roll : 1..8 | null
    + amount : integer | null
    + state : PENDING | ROLLED | CREDITED | FAILED
    + attempts : integer
    + failureReason : string | null
  }
  class ExperienceRewardPolicy <<política pura>> {
    + rewardFor(roll : 1..8) : integer
    ..ÚNICO dueño de 10 × 1,2^(1d8)..
  }
  ExperienceRewardPolicy ..> ExperienceReward : calcula amount
}

package "Player / Inventory" #FFF7EE {
  class ExperienceGrant <<ledger insert-only>> {
    + operationId : string (clave _id)
    + ownerId : string
    + heroId : string
    + amount : integer
    + roll : 1..8
    + enrollmentId : string
    + createdAt : Date
  }
  class HeroProgression <<HU-08, ya implementado>> {
    + level : 1..8
    + currentXp : integer
    + awardExperience(amount)
    + thresholdForNextLevel()
  }
  ExperienceGrant ..> HeroProgression : acredita en la misma transacción
}

ExperienceReward --> ExperienceRoll : consume (no la posee)
ExperienceReward --> ExperienceGrant : produce (idempotente por operationId)
ExperienceReward ..> HeroProgression : NUNCA la copia\n(estado de otro contexto)

note bottom of ExperienceRewardPolicy
  La fórmula vive SOLO aquí.
  Combat no la conoce y
  Player/Inventory no la aplica.
end note
@enduml
